        "event": {
          "timestamp": "2026-03-17T20:36:32.794Z",
          "hook_event_name": "UserPromptSubmit",
          "session_id": "f24bf9ae-3acf-4efa-bd08-ca3a80e127a5",
          "prompt": "Create the `semio/studio` bundle. This is a new npm package that owns all Y.js persistence providers and re-exports Y from yjs.\n\n## Context\n- The workspace root is `/workspaces/semio/`\n- There is already an empty file at `/workspaces/semio/semio/studio/studio.ts`\n- The root `package.json` workspaces array needs `\"semio/studio\"` added\n- The `semio-elements/ui/elements.tsx` currently exports: `export * as Y from \"yjs\"` and `export { IndexeddbPersistence } from \"y-indexeddb\"` (lines 10321-10322)\n- The sketchpad's `shared.ts` currently has persistence provider code that needs to move to studio.ts\n- The sketchpad's `shared.ts` currently imports Y from `../../../semio-elements/ui`\n\n## What you MUST do\n\n### 1. Create `semio/studio/package.json`\n```json\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"../../node_modules/nx/schemas/project-schema.json\",\n  \"projectType\": \"library\",\n  \"name\": \"@semio/studio\",\n  \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"description\": \"semio · studio — Y.js CRDT runtime and kit persistence providers\",\n  \"exports\": {\n    \".\": \"./studio.ts\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"yjs\": \"^13.6.29\",\n    \"y-indexeddb\": \"^9.0.12\"\n  },\n  \"author\": {\n    \"name\": \"Ueli Saluz\",\n    \"email\": \"ueli@semio-tech.com\",\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/usalu\"\n  },\n  \"license\": \"AGPL-3.0-or-later\",\n  \"repository\": {\n    \"type\": \"git\",\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/usalu/semio.git\",\n    \"directory\": \"semio/studio\"\n  },\n  \"bundleKind\": \"lib\"\n}\n```\n\n### 2. Write `semio/studio/studio.ts`\nThis file MUST contain:\n\na) Re-export Y from yjs:\n```typescript\nexport * as Y from \"yjs\";\n```\n\nb) Re-export IndexeddbPersistence:\n```typescript\nexport { IndexeddbPersistence } from \"y-indexeddb\";\n```\n\nc) The `PersistenceProvider` interface (copy from shared.ts):\n```typescript\nexport interface PersistenceProvider {\n  once(event: \"synced\", callback: () =\u003e void): void;\n  on(event: \"synced\", callback: () =\u003e void): void;\n  destroy(): void;\n}\n```\n\nd) The `PersistenceFactory` type:\n```typescript\nexport type PersistenceFactory = (doc: Y.Doc, key: string) =\u003e PersistenceProvider;\n```\n\ne) `JsonFileAdapter` interface:\n```typescript\nexport interface JsonFileAdapter {\n  read(key: string): Promise\u003cstring | null\u003e;\n  write(key: string, json: string): Promise\u003cvoid\u003e;\n}\n```\n\nf) `SqliteAdapter` interface:\n```typescript\nexport interface SqliteAdapter {\n  read(key: string): Promise\u003cUint8Array | null\u003e;\n  write(key: string, data: Uint8Array): Promise\u003cvoid\u003e;\n}\n```\n\ng) `YDocBinaryPersistenceProvider` class (the full implementation from shared.ts)\n\nh) `createIndexeddbPersistenceFactory` function:\n```typescript\nexport function createIndexeddbPersistenceFactory(): PersistenceFactory {\n  return (doc: Y.Doc, key: string) =\u003e new IndexeddbPersistence(key, doc);\n}\n```\n\ni) `createJsonFilePersistenceFactory` function (the full implementation from shared.ts)\n\nj) `createSqliteFolderPersistenceFactory` function (the full implementation from shared.ts)\n\nThe file MUST follow the project's header/region conventions:\n- Start with `#region 🔖Header` with the semiorepo link, copyright, license, and file summary\n- Use `#region 🔖Exports` for the re-exports\n- Use `#region 🔖PersistenceProviders` for the interfaces, classes, and factory functions\n- End each region with the corresponding `#endregion`\n\n### 3. Add `\"semio/studio\"` to root `package.json` workspaces\nThe root package.json is at `/workspaces/semio/package.json`. Add `\"semio/studio\"` to the workspaces array (add it after `\"semio/sketchpad\"`).\n\n### 4. Create `semio/studio/tsconfig.json`\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"lib\": [\"ES2022\"],\n    \"strict\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"Bundler\",\n    \"esModuleInterop\": true,\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  },\n  \"include\": [\"studio.ts\"]\n}\n```\n\n### 5. Create `semio/studio/README.md`\nShort README with:\n```markdown\n---\nname: studio\nkind: bundle\nemoji: 👥\nsummary: Y.js CRDT runtime and kit persistence providers for semio sketchpad.\n---\n\n### Summary\nY.js CRDT runtime and kit persistence providers for semio sketchpad.\n\n### Specs\n- Re-exports Y and IndexeddbPersistence from yjs/y-indexeddb\n- Provides PersistenceProvider interface and PersistenceFactory type\n- Implements IndexedDB, JSON file, and SQLite folder persistence factories\n- YDocBinaryPersistenceProvider uses Y.encodeStateAsUpdate/applyUpdate for CRDT round-tripping\n```\n\n### 6. Run `npm install` from the workspace root to link the new package\n\nAfter creating all files, run `cd /workspaces/semio \u0026\u0026 npm install` to link the workspace.\n\nThen verify with `cd /workspaces/semio/semio/studio \u0026\u0026 npx tsc --noEmit` to check TypeScript compilation.\n\n## IMPORTANT\n- Do NOT modify any files outside of `semio/studio/` and the root `package.json`\n- Do NOT open or close tickets — just do the work\n- Check the result of `npm install` and `tsc --noEmit` and report any errors\n- The file ID/link convention uses format: `[👤semio👥studio💻studio](semiorepo://p/u/semio/b/l/studio/f/studio.ts)`\n- Use `kind` instead of `type` for naming conventions",
